---
import ContactEmail from "@/components/legal/ContactEmail.astro";
import LegalSection from "@/components/legal/LegalSection.astro";
import OperatorInfo from "@/components/legal/OperatorInfo.astro";
import { legal } from "@/config/legal";
import { turnstile } from "@/config/site";
import { sentence } from "@/config/placeholders";
import Legal from "@/layouts/Legal.astro";
import Brand from "@/components/ui/Brand.astro";
---

<Legal title="Privacy Policy – Snugglegum™" description="How Snugglegum™ handles your data: newsletter sign-up with double opt-in via MailerLite, cookies, retention and your rights under the GDPR." path="/privacy" heading="Privacy Policy">
  <LegalSection title="1. Controller">
    <p>The controller under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:</p>
    <OperatorInfo />
    <p>
      Contact for privacy matters:
      <ContactEmail field="privacyEmail" />
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="2. Overview">
    <p>This website is a pre-launch page for <Brand />. It has no user accounts, no shop and no comment function. We process personal data only in the cases described below.</p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="3. Hosting and server log files">
    <p>
      The website is hosted by{sentence(legal.hostingProvider.display ?? "")}When you visit the site, the hosting provider's servers process technical data that your browser transmits: IP address, date and time, requested address, referrer, and browser and operating system information. This data is
      kept in server log files.
    </p>
    <p>Purpose: delivering the website and keeping it secure. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (our legitimate interest in stable and secure operation). Retention:{sentence(legal.logRetention.display ?? "")}</p>
    <p>
      The sign-up form is handled by a small program that runs at our hosting provider (a serverless function). To protect it from abuse, for example mass sign-ups by bots or other people's addresses, it keeps a short-lived technical fingerprint of your IP address and of the email address you enter: a one-way
      hash from which neither can be read back. It is held in the provider's cache for at most 10 minutes and is used only to limit repeated attempts. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (our legitimate interest in protecting the form and the list from abuse).
    </p>
    <p>The same program keeps a plain counter of sign-ups (a number, without any personal data). Section 5 describes what your browser stores so the thank-you page can show your number.</p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="4. Fonts and external resources">
    <p>All fonts and images are served from our own server. Your browser does not contact Google Fonts or any content delivery network when you load this website. When you submit the newsletter form, your browser sends it to our own server, which passes it on to MailerLite (see sections 6 and 7).</p>
    {
      turnstile.siteKey && (
        <p>
          To tell people from bots, the sign-up form uses Cloudflare Turnstile. When you first click into the form, your browser loads a script from Cloudflare (challenges.cloudflare.com), so Cloudflare receives your IP address and technical browser data. This check normally runs without any action on your part. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (our
          legitimate interest in protecting the form from abuse). Cloudflare's privacy policy is available at <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a>.
        </p>
      )
    }
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="5. Cookies and local storage" id="cookies">
    <p>
      We do not set any cookies. When you make a choice in the cookie settings, we store it in your browser's local storage (entry name "sg-cookie-consent") together with a version number and a timestamp. This lets us remember your choice so we do not ask you on every visit. It is strictly necessary
      to provide that function, so it does not require your consent. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR and section 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG.
    </p>
    <p>
      We currently use no analytics or marketing tools. If we add such tools later, they will load only after you consent, and we will update this policy first. You can change your choice at any time with the "Cookie settings" button in the footer. You can also delete the stored entry in your
      browser settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you sign up, your browser also keeps your founding number for a moment in its session storage (entry name "sg-founding-number") so the thank-you page can show it. The entry disappears when you close the tab or window. It is strictly necessary to provide that function, so it does not require your consent.
      Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR and section 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="6. Newsletter and launch list">
    <p>
      If you sign up for the launch list, we process the email address you enter, the versions and flavors you tick, the flavor you suggest if you type one, your confirmation that you meet the minimum age and agree to the emails (with the time you gave it), the campaign tags of the link you came from
      (if any), and the technical data needed to prove your consent (for example the IP address used when you confirm). Your sign-up also gets a running number. We use this data to send you launch news, early access and the pre-launch offer, and to take your flavor wishes into account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Legal basis: your consent, Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR. The consent checkbox is not pre-ticked, and nothing is sent before you press the sign-up button. We use double opt-in: after you sign up, we send a confirmation email. Your address is added as confirmed only after you click the link in that email.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can withdraw your consent at any time with effect for the future, for example with the unsubscribe link in every email or by contacting us. Withdrawing does not affect the lawfulness of processing before the withdrawal. Providing your email address is voluntary. Without it, we cannot add
      you to the list.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="7. MailerLite (processor)">
    <p>
      We use MailerLite to collect sign-ups and send emails. Provider:{sentence(legal.mailerLiteEntity.display ?? "")}MailerLite processes your data on our behalf under a data processing agreement pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR. Its own privacy policy is available at
      <a href="https://www.mailerlite.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">mailerlite.com/legal/privacy-policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you press the sign-up button, your browser sends your entries to our own server, which passes them on to MailerLite. MailerLite therefore receives them from our server. When you click the confirmation link in the email, your browser contacts MailerLite directly, so MailerLite then also receives your
      IP address.
    </p>
    {legal.mailerLiteTracking.display && <p>{legal.mailerLiteTracking.display}</p>}
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="8. Recipients">
    <p>Recipients of your data are our hosting provider{turnstile.siteKey && " (including Cloudflare for the bot check)"} and MailerLite, each only as far as needed for the purposes above. We do not sell your personal data.</p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="9. Transfers to third countries">
    <p>MailerLite may process data outside the European Economic Area, including in the United States. Where that happens, the transfer relies on:{sentence(legal.transferMechanism.display ?? "")}</p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="10. Retention">
    <p>
      We keep your newsletter data until you unsubscribe or withdraw your consent. After that we delete it, except for a record of your consent and its withdrawal, which we keep as long as needed to prove them (Art. 6(1)(f) and Art. 7(1) GDPR) or as the law requires. Server log data is deleted as
      stated in section 3.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="11. Your rights">
    <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access your data (Art. 15),</li>
      <li>have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16),</li>
      <li>have your data erased (Art. 17),</li>
      <li>restrict processing (Art. 18),</li>
      <li>receive your data in a portable format (Art. 20),</li>
      <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21),</li>
      <li>withdraw consent at any time (Art. 7(3)).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To use these rights, contact us at the address in section 1. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. The competent authority is:{sentence(legal.supervisoryAuthority.display ?? "")}</p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="12. Automated decisions">
    <p>We do not use automated decision-making or profiling.</p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="13. US state privacy rights">
    <p>We do not sell your personal data, and we do not use it for cross-context behavioral advertising.</p>
    {legal.usStatePrivacy.display && <p>{legal.usStatePrivacy.display}</p>}
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="14. Changes">
    <p>We update this policy when the website or the law changes. The current version is always on this page.</p>
  </LegalSection>
</Legal>
